---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Martín Ramírez Espinosa: Electronic Engineering and Mathematics student working across ML systems, signal processing, and reliable software."
>
  <header class="page-intro shell section about-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>I like difficult systems more when their assumptions are visible.</h1>
    <p>
      I’m Martín, an Electronic Engineering and Mathematics student at the Universidad Nacional de
      Colombia in Manizales. I’m an official member of the <a
        href="https://scienti.minciencias.gov.co/gruplac/jsp/visualiza/visualizagr.jsp?nro=00000000001375"
        >Control and Digital Signal Processing Group (GCPDS)</a
      >, part of the <a href="https://amalvarezme.github.io/LaboratorioIA_UNAL/"
        >LIA-UNAL research ecosystem</a
      >, and build across machine learning, research infrastructure, local-first products, and
      embedded audio systems.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="section section-rule shell about-grid" aria-labelledby="approach-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Approach</p>
      <h2 id="approach-heading">Research thinking, production discipline.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>
        My projects usually begin with a question that needs both theory and implementation: whether
        a tokenizer comparison is actually fair, whether a research assistant can preserve the
        passage behind a claim, whether personal analytics can work without surrendering data, or
        where an audio system’s hardware and firmware contracts should meet.
      </p>
      <p>
        I turn those questions into explicit interfaces, tests, reproducible artifacts, and honest
        limits. I care about the behavior at boundaries—model output entering domain logic, archives
        crossing a filesystem parser, remote evidence becoming local data, or software controlling
        physical hardware.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    class="section section-rule shell capability-section"
    aria-labelledby="capabilities-heading"
  >
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Engineering range</p>
        <h2 id="capabilities-heading">Capabilities grounded in shipped work.</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="capability-grid">
      <article>
        <h3>Machine learning & research</h3><p>
          PyTorch, language-model fundamentals, retrieval, evaluation design, evidence synthesis,
          and reproducible experiments.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Software systems</h3><p>
          Python, Rust, TypeScript, React, SQLite, browser automation, terminal interfaces, typed
          adapters, and local-first design.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Signals & embedded engineering</h3><p>
          Digital signal processing, C/C++, STM32, USB audio, codec integration, electronics, and
          mixed hardware/software architecture.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Reliability</h3><p>
          Strict typing, security boundaries, CI, branch coverage, fail-closed parsing, provenance,
          and limitations treated as product behavior.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule shell about-grid" aria-labelledby="collaboration-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Open-source collaboration</p>
      <h2 id="collaboration-heading">Work accepted beyond my own repositories.</h2>
    </div>
    <article class="collaboration-card">
      <p class="eyebrow">Merged · March 2026</p>
      <h3>ANE2 spectral node-calibration runtime</h3>
      <p>
        I integrated a self-contained calibration runtime into ANE2-Calibration-SDR, including
        artifact provenance, PSD-frame calibration, campaign materialization, and integration tests.
        The upstream maintainer approved and merged the contribution.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/dramirezbe/ANE2-Calibration-SDR/pull/4"
        >Inspect the merged pull request <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
      >
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule shell opportunity" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
      <h2 id="contact-heading">Let’s work on something that has to be right.</h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>
        I’m available for remote internships, part-time engineering roles, and focused contracts
        alongside my studies in Colombia, particularly across research engineering, ML systems,
        applied AI, and reliable software.
      </p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/Martin_Ramirez_Espinosa_Resume.pdf">View résumé</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="mailto:maramirezes@unal.edu.co">Email Martín</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="https://github.com/almondsun">GitHub profile</a>
        <a
          class="button button-secondary"
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/martin-ramirez-espinosa/">LinkedIn profile</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
